            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="0681" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12525.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. The whole diplomatic corps attended today the official reception of
                    Provisional President; Spanish Minister as Dean of Corps made usual address. The
                    President in his reply confirmed his good intentions to promote the pacification
                    of country and frankly added that his person would in no way be an obstacle to
                    it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
